sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/murrays-law-vascular-optimality--grok-4-7--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Derive the junction exponent from a stated cost" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/murrays-law-vascular-optimality> ;
    dct:description "Minimize, for one vessel, a Poiseuille pumping cost proportional to Q squared over r to the fourth plus a blood-volume cost proportional to r squared. Prove the optimum is r cubed proportional to Q. At a junction with Q_parent = Q_1 + Q_2 and the same constant of proportionality, prove r_parent cubed equals r_1 cubed plus r_2 cubed. Then replace the resistance exponent by a parameter b and the flow exponent by a parameter a, and prove the junction exponent is (b + 2) / a for a volume cost proportional to r squared. State which (a, b) would yield 7/3, and do not assert that turbulent flow has those exponents unless the algebra produces them from a stated friction law. The laminar cubic law and the general exponent are the theorems." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A no-sorry cubic junction law under Poiseuille-plus-volume cost, and a general exponent (b + 2) / a with the unique (a, b) pair that equals 7/3." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The cubic law does not follow from those costs, or more than one (a, b) pair on the stated family yields 7/3. The derivation would then not pin down the turbulent alternative." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/formalization" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Define Poiseuille power and volume cost. 2. Prove the cubic optimum and the junction law. 3. Generalize to resistance exponent b and flow exponent a. 4. Solve for the (a, b) pair that would give junction exponent 7/3. 5. Audit axioms." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-13> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-03> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.78.4.431> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/murrays-law-vascular-optimality> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Does real vasculature obey Murray's law?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207> dct:title "The Physiological Principle of Minimum Work" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Murray 1926, The physiological principle of minimum work I" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1085/jgp.78.4.431> dct:title "On connecting large vessels to small. The meaning of Murray's law." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Sherman 1981, On connecting large vessels to small" .
}

